Multi-dimensional time series forecasting is essential for monitoring indoor micro-environments and other critical systems. Sequential modeling approaches struggle with high computational complexity, while many current machine learning methods fail to generalize across multiple dimensions. To address these issues, this work proposes a new sparse structure for frequency domain analysis. First, we apply sparsity constraints to more effectively extract signal frequency characteristics. Second, we decompose the signal into multiple segments. Third, we design a sparse structure of convolutional auto-encoders to forecast each segment simultaneously across all dimensions. Finally, we reconstruct the long sequence by superimposing these predictions. Both theoretical analysis and experimental results confirm the model's enhanced efficiency and accuracy in multi-dimensional forecasting compared to sequential models and other current methods. Keywords: Multi-dimensional Time Series Forecasting; Long Sequence Forecasting; Sparsity; Fourier Transform; Piecewise Convolicutional Network;

